                <head>372. Memorandum From Secretary of State Vance to President Carter<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d372-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1979-11-17">November 17, 1979</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>[Omitted here is material unrelated to Pakistan.]</p>
                <p>3. <hi rendition="#italic">Pakistan:</hi> During a recent trip to Western Europe,
                    Gerry Smith asked senior officials in the UK, France, FRG and the Netherlands to
                    consider telling Pakistan, as we have, that a nuclear test by Pakistan would
                    foreshadow major changes in bilateral relations. Gerry did not find support for
                    this approach, and his interlocutors were also pessimistic that any combination
                    of available incentives or disincentives would influence Pakistan’s nuclear
                    course. His visit to Western Europe immediately followed that of Hua Guofeng,
                    who had emphasized the need to bolster Pakistan against Soviet activities in the
                    area.</p>
                <p>[Omitted here is material unrelated to Pakistan.]</p>
            </div>
